{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "The destination-address classes of the gateway: for each address, the class it has and whether it is public (globally routable unicast, the only class a gateway dials without a rule). The Node host (src/address-class.mjs, run by test/address-guard-export.test.mjs) and the Rust wsh-server (crates/wsh-core/src/gateway/address_class.rs) both run this file, so the two implementations agree address by address. An IPv6 address that wraps an IPv4 one (IPv4-mapped ::ffff:0:0/96, NAT64 64:ff9b::/96, 6to4 2002::/16) has the class of the IPv4 address it carries; Teredo (2001::/32) is teredo whatever it carries; the IPv4-compatible form ::a.b.c.d and the local-use NAT64 prefix 64:ff9b:1::/48 are reserved; only 2000::/3 is global unicast. Each group lists the first and last address of a range and the addresses just outside it.",
